 "result": "Call order (this repo is a Flask-like framework, \"tessel\"):\n\n1. `Tessel.__call__` → `Tessel.wsgi_entry`, `src/tessel/app.py:1618` and `:1566`. It calls `run_full_request` at `:1597`.\n2. `Tessel.run_full_request`, `src/tessel/app.py:992`. It ends with `return self.finalize_request(ctx, rv)` at `:1019`. Error paths reach `finalize_request` too, from `route_unhandled_fault` at `:948`.\n3. `Tessel.finalize_request`, `src/tessel/app.py:1021`. It calls `make_response` (`:1224`) and then `finalize_reply`.\n4. `Tessel.finalize_reply`, `src/tessel/app.py:1394`. It runs the after-request functions. Then, at `:1415-1416`, it calls `persist_session` if `session_interface.is_null_session(ctx._get_session())` is false.\n5. `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session`, `src/tessel/sessions.py:337`. It does the cookie work:\n   - **Vary header:** it adds `Vary: Cookie` if the session was accessed.\n   - **Empty, modified session:** it calls `response.delete_cookie` (`:356`).\n   - **Otherwise:** it checks `cookie_needs_write`, then signs the data with `make_signer(app).dumps(dict(session))` (`:373`) and calls `response.set_cookie(...)` (`:374`).\n\nThe default `session_interface` is `SignedCookieSessionInterface()`, set at `src/tessel/app.py:250`.",
